# PREBOOTNOTIFY_COMPONENT_STATE enumeration

This enumeration is used by the [**PREBOOTNOTIFY\_COMPONENT**](https://docs.microsoft.com/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/content/preboot/ns-preboot-_prebootnotify_component) structure.

**Note**  This enumeration is available in Windows 10, version 1507 and later versions.


## -description

This enumeration represents the possible states of a kernel component that is being notified by the PrebootExecution.

## -enum-fields

### -field PREBOOTNOTIFY_COMPONENT_STATE_INVALID

The component state is invalid.

### -field PREBOOTNOTIFY_COMPONENT_STATE_BEFORE_INITIALIZATION 

The component has not been initialized yet.

### -field PREBOOTNOTIFY_COMPONENT_STATE_RUNNING

The component is running.

### -field PREBOOTNOTIFY_COMPONENT_STATE_POST_EXIT

The component has exited and is being cleaned up. The component may be unloaded or the system may be in the process of rebooting.

## -remarks

The PREBOOTNOTIFY_COMPONENT_STATE values are used to provide the PrebootExecution with the current state of a component. 

## -see-also

